title: 'tdgovernance: Data Governance Concept Template for Transdisciplinary Research'
version: 0.1.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23062613
abstract: Template for a Data Governance Concept in transdisciplinary research, developed
  in the FAIRqual project. The underlying idea of the Data Governance Concept is to
  make data governance a functional element of a transdisciplinary approach that is
  introduced at the start of a project for both researchers and practitioners. The
  template guides a project team with questions through three phases. The phases shift
  from data governance, to data management, where data are generated and handled day-to-day,
  and eventually to data stewardship in the later phases of a project. The template
  is available as DOCX and Markdown, together with a figure of the three phases and
  the roles of researchers and practitioners in each phase.
